Related, but not the same: #69101 (a `Nullable<T>` struct doesn't get its XML description).

### Describe the bug

Schema transformers are called for a property whose type is a nullable struct (`Fee?`), but not for anything inside
it. The same struct used as a non-nullable property (`Fee`) has all its members transformed.

### Expected Behavior

Schema transformers run for the members of a nullable struct, as they do for the members of the same struct when it isn't nullable.

### Steps To Reproduce

```csharp
var builder = WebApplication.CreateBuilder(args);
builder.Services.AddOpenApi(options => options.AddSchemaTransformer((schema, context, _) =>
{
    Console.WriteLine($"{context.JsonTypeInfo.Type.Name} {context.JsonPropertyInfo?.Name}");
    return Task.CompletedTask;
}));

var app = builder.Build();
app.MapOpenApi();
app.MapGet("/fee", () => new FeeHolder(new Fee(1, [2], new FeeDetail("detail"))));
app.Run();

record FeeHolder(Fee? Fee);
readonly record struct Fee(int Count, int[] Amounts, FeeDetail Detail);
record FeeDetail(string Name);
```

Requesting `/openapi/v1.json` logs `FeeHolder`, then `Nullable1 fee`, and nothing for `count`, `amounts` (or its items), `detail` or `name`. With `Fee Fee` (not nullable) they are all logged.

### .NET Version

Reproduced on 10.0.15; the same code is on `main`.

